s two or three, so a table seeded with one row passes REQ-3 and fails REQ-4 (and REQ-4 otherwise repeats REQ-3).\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-1.3 lists every path with an /api prefix (e.g. POST /api/auth/sign-in, GET /api/sample-data), but the anchored contract declares /auth/sign-in and /sample-data, and no servers/base-path anchor backs the prefix, which contradicts I-1's 'exactly as it is written'.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-1.3 lists about 45 operations but only two contract anchors exist, so nothing anchors the list's paths or shows it covers 'every operation' in contracts/openapi.yaml.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"rubric\": 5,\n   \"severity\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The contract operations POST /sample-data/load, /reset and /replace put demo data in at runtime, which conflicts with REQ-5's 'insert no demo rows' when Seed:Demo is false and with I-4's 'runs that file only when Seed:Demo is true', and the spec never reconciles them.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"rubric\": 1,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The spec never says what sample-data reset/replace do to non-demo operational rows, the test-only fixture account, or the pre-existing rows that REQ-2/Q-2 must preserve.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"AC-2.1 needs application tables created in a database that already has an unrelated table, but the anchored startup uses EnsureCreated(), which does nothing when any table exists; the spec names no schema-initialization or migration mechanism and no upgrade path for databases EnsureCreated already built.\",\n   \"reqId\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"rubric\": 6,\n   \"severity\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"finding\": \"The EARS forbids changing 'any pre-existing database contents', while Q-2 