I shall populate each application table with two or three believable sample rows based on examples in contracts/openapi.yaml.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.3333333333333333\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Seed:Demo is false, the database has no operational or demo rows, and a test-only account fixture provisions a valid non-demo account with the contract-required authorization state directly in PostgreSQL, separately from demo seed data.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The protected list response statuses and fields conform to the contract without requiring a demo-seeded record.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client signs in using the fixture credentials and authenticates protected list requests with the returned authorization, including requests valid for an empty operational data state.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The App database has no operational or demo rows, Seed:Demo is false, and a test-only account fixture separate from demo seed data provisions a principal with the permissions required by the protected lists.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Every application-data table has a demo row count of zero, and the response lists contain no demo-seeded records.\",\n     \"when\": \"The application starts, the client signs in with the fixture account, and the client requests database-backed protected lists using the returned authorization.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A clean PostgreSQL database, application configuration Seed:Demo=false, and a test-only account fixture separate from demo seed data with the permissions required by protected list operations.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The demo-data row count is zero and the list responses contain no demo rows.\",\n     \"when\": \"The application starts, a client signs in with the fixture account and authenticates list API requests with the returned authorization, and a test queries the application tables.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 24,\n     \"lineStart\": 22,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        db.Database.EnsureCreated();\\n        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\\\"Seed:Demo\\\")) SeedData.Run(db);\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 17,\n     \"lineStart\": 12,\n     \"path\": \"App.Tests/HealthTests.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"    [Fact]\\n    public async Task ApiIsUp()\\n    {\\n        var res = await _factory.CreateClient().GetAsync(\\\"/\\\");\\n        Assert.Equal(HttpStatusCode.OK, res.StatusCode);\\n    }\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is false at application startup, the Feedlot Operations API shall skip SeedData.Run and insert no demo rows, and serve contract operations without requiring demo seed rows, including protected list requests authenticated using a test-only account fixture separate from demo seed data.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-4\",\n    \"Q-7\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The repository implementation is complete.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The review finds API and API documentation surfaces but no product-facing screens or frontend implementation.\",\n     \"when\": \"A person reviews its exposed web surfaces and frontend files.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API application built from this repository.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n     \"level\": \"manual\",\n     \"then\": \"The screen shows API health or API documentation and does not show feedlot product screens.\",\n     \"when\": \"A person inspects its browser-accessible surfaces